# XSH 2.4.4 Signal Effects on Other Functions
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.

assertion  XSH.2.4.4-signal-effects.001
anchor     functions/V2_chap02.html#2.4.4
class      required
since      1988
says       A child blocked in read() on an empty pipe that gets SIGTERM at
           SIG_DFL is terminated by it (within 10 s); read() does not
           return.
test       t/001-terminate-no-return.c

assertion  XSH.2.4.4-signal-effects.002
anchor     functions/V2_chap02.html#2.4.4
class      required
since      2001
says       A child blocked in read() on an empty pipe is stopped with SIGSTOP
           and continued with SIGCONT; read() goes on waiting and, when a
           byte is written, returns it (not -1/EINTR).
test       t/002-stop-continue.c

assertion  XSH.2.4.4-signal-effects.003
anchor     functions/V2_chap02.html#2.4.4
class      required
since      2024
says       A child blocked in read() on an empty pipe, with SIGUSR1 at SIG_IGN,
           SIGCHLD and SIGWINCH at SIG_DFL (ignored by default) and SIGUSR2
           caught but blocked, is sent all four; read() goes on waiting and
           returns the byte written afterwards, and the SIGUSR2 handler has
           not run by then.
note       SIGWINCH is new in Issue 8.
test       t/003-ignored-blocked-no-effect.c
